ious stance widths, foot placement angles and level of experience on knee, hip and trunk motion and loading","sourcePublisher":"BMC Sports Science, Medicine and Rehabilitation","sourceKind":"peer_reviewed_research","evidenceQuality":86,"claims":["Stance and foot angle change lower-limb and trunk motion/loading in squat tasks, so use an individually comfortable foot-supported base.","A valid cycle maintains a controlled hinge/contact, comfortable squat entry, declared reach, controlled stand, and reset; do not create range through forced lumbar motion or momentum."]},{"sectionKey":"difficulty","sourceUrl":"https://www.nsca.com/globalassets/about/position-statements/position_stand_youth_resistance_training---2009.pdf","sourceTitle":"Youth Resistance Training: Updated Position Statement Paper From the NSCA","sourcePublisher":"National Strength and Conditioning Association","sourceKind":"professional_standard","evidenceQuality":88,"claims":["Difficulty is exercise complexity and physical difficulty only; it does not classify athlete skill, proficiency, age, or readiness.","The combined hinge, squat entry, overhead reach, and stand raise coordination demand despite low external load. Independent calibration remains required."]},{"sectionKey":"load_fatigue_recovery","sourceUrl":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/26642915/","sourceTitle":"Acute effects of muscle stretching on physical performance, range of motion, and injury incidence in healthy active individuals: a systematic review","sourcePublisher":"Applied Physiology, Nutrition, and Metabolism","sourceKind":"peer_reviewed_research","evidenceQuality":90,"claims":["Acute mobility responses depend on dose, timing, and following activity; no universal readiness, recovery, or performance outcome is claimed.","Track repetitions, reach side/order, stance, range, contact, breath, compensation, symptoms, and downstream work rather than assigning a universal recovery rule."]},{"sectionKey":"constraints","sourceUrl":"https://www.